Q: How to get a remote JPG from a URL using USER and Password? A: <p>You cannot do this by using your same task. You need to create another asyntask&lt;> that will fetch image for you and return bitmap. I done this before too. Use this code for this..</p>

<pre><code>Bitmap image = null;

    @Override
    protected Bitmap doInBackground(String... params) {
        try {
// param[0] would be replaced with your image path.
            image = BitmapFactory.decodeStream((InputStream)new URL(params[0]).getContent());
        } catch (MalformedURLException e) {
            Log.e("MalformedURLException",e.toString());
        } catch (IOException e) {
            Log.e("IOException",e.toString());
        }       
        return image;       
    }
</code></pre>

<p>Hope, again it will work for you.</p>

Q: Enter a code branch every ten percent till 100 percent A: <p>I might misunderstand you, but it seems like you're trying to do something extremely simple more complex than it needs to be. What about this?</p>

<pre><code>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 100; i++)
{
    if (i % 10 == 0)
    {
        // Here, you can do what you want - this will happen 
        // every ten iterations ("percent")
    }
}
</code></pre>

<p>Or, if your entire code enters from somewhere else (so no loop in this scope), the important part is the <code>i % 10 == 0</code>.</p>

Q: Take integer inputs till the user enters 0 and print the sum of all numbers (HINT: while loop) (coding language:- JAVA) A: <pre><code>public class Input_n_until_enter0 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        java.util.Scanner scanner = new java.util.Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println(&quot;Enter number or enter 0 to finish:&quot;);
        int sum = 0, count = 0;
        while (true) {
            int n = scanner.nextInt();
            count++;
            if (n == 0) {
                break;
            }
            sum += n;
        }
        System.out.println(&quot;Total sum is: &quot; + sum);
        System.out.println(&quot;Count of entered numbers: &quot;+(count-1));
        System.out.println(&quot;Program Ended!&quot;);
        scanner.close();
    }
}
</code></pre>

